A||||3||Cozmo||Blown head gasket?||||1||
Z||000000||Cozmo||03-06-2001||08:28 AM||||Hi list,<BR>   After working on getting the '85 2M6 Targa on the road for the first time since I got it there seems to still be a "problem". I replaced the water pump, tapped out a stripped water pump bolt, repaired the brake vaccuum boost and fixed the shift cables.<BR>The car starts fine, idles steady at about 1000 rpm but with a steady miss. It will idle like that for a long time with no problems, but if you drive it for about 20 min. white smoke (seems like steam) pours from the exhaust. There is no water in the oil, when you run the car with the rad cap off there seems to be normal water movement and no "combustion leak" into the water jacket. Besides the miss, the car seems to run pretty good.  I haven't done a compression check yet (this weekend) is there any other things I can check to see if I have a blown head gasket or maybe something else wrong??<BR>Thanks, <P>------------------<BR>Cozmo<BR>'87 Dead Duke__________'85 2M6 Targa<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bothfierossig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||03-06-2001||12:25 PM||||The compression test will hopefully tell you for sure, but it sounds odd. The fact that it's getting spunky after 20 minutes would initially point my towards either the cold-run loop, or the coolant system. But the mist like white exhaust sounds much more like a head gasket. The only other thing I can think of off the top of my head it the initial reset. once the computer loses power, you have to drive it above 45 mph for a few miles (or something like that) to get the comp to calibrate. hope for the best, good luck this weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||03-06-2001||03:45 PM||||My car did the same thing and it was a blown head gasket. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cozmo||03-06-2001||06:17 PM||||Yeah, I'm afraid it's a head gasket too...<BR>I knew it had cooling problems when I got it.<BR>Well, I've gone from 2 running Fieros to none in a week <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Cozmo||||reg||1
